/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · Esther chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("esther", [
{n:1, name:"The Queen Who Refused",
 seal:{ref:"Esther 1:19",verse:"If it please the king, let there go a royal commandment from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, that it be not altered, That Vashti come no more before king Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate unto another that is better than she."},
 facts:["Did you know Ahasuerus ruled 127 provinces, a realm so vast that the decree about Vashti had to be published to every people in their own language (Esther 1:1, 22)?","Did you know that among the Persians and Medes a royal law once written could not be altered, which is why Vashti's dismissal stood forever, and why later decrees in this book carry such dreadful weight (Esther 1:19)?","Did you know the king's 180-day display of his riches ended with a seven-day feast for everyone in Shushan, great and small, in a court hung with white, green, and blue, with beds of gold and silver (Esther 1:4-6)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"How far did the kingdom of Ahasuerus stretch?", options:["From India even unto Ethiopia","From Egypt even unto Babylon","From Greece even unto Persia","From Shushan even unto Jerusalem"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:1",verse:"Now it came to pass in the days of Ahasuerus, (this is Ahasuerus which reigned, from India even unto Ethiopia, over an hundred and seven and twenty provinces:)", insight:"An empire of 127 provinces, and God had planted His people inside every one of them."},
{q:"How many provinces did Ahasuerus rule over?", options:["An hundred and seven and twenty","Sixty and six","Two hundred and forty","An hundred and ten"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:1",verse:"Now it came to pass in the days of Ahasuerus, (this is Ahasuerus which reigned, from India even unto Ethiopia, over an hundred and seven and twenty provinces:)", insight:"Scripture counts the provinces because the size of the stage matters for the size of the deliverance."},
{q:"Where did King Ahasuerus sit on the throne of his kingdom?", options:["In Shushan the palace","In Jerusalem","In Babylon","In Ecbatana"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:2",verse:"That in those days, when the king Ahasuerus sat on the throne of his kingdom, which was in Shushan the palace,", insight:"Power sat in Shushan, but the true throne in this story belongs to the God never named in it."},
{q:"In which year of his reign did Ahasuerus make his great feast?", options:["In the third year","In the first year","In the seventh year","In the twelfth year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:3",verse:"In the third year of his reign, he made a feast unto all his princes and his servants; the power of Persia and Media, the nobles and princes of the provinces, being before him:", insight:"The feast that started everything came early in his reign; pride announces itself long before it falls."},
{q:"For how many days did the king show the riches of his glorious kingdom?", options:["An hundred and fourscore days","Seven days","Forty days","A whole year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:4",verse:"When he shewed the riches of his glorious kingdom and the honour of his excellent majesty many days, even an hundred and fourscore days.", insight:"Six months of showing off; wealth displayed that long becomes worship."},
{q:"How long did the feast for all the people of Shushan last?", options:["Seven days","Three days","A full month","One evening"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:5",verse:"And when these days were expired, the king made a feast unto all the people that were present in Shushan the palace, both unto great and small, seven days, in the court of the garden of the king’s palace;", insight:"The king fed a whole city for a week; generosity is good, but this generosity had an audience."},
{q:"What were the beds in the palace court made of?", options:["Gold and silver","Wood and ivory","Stone and cedar","Bronze and iron"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:6",verse:"Where were white, green, and blue, hangings, fastened with cords of fine linen and purple to silver rings and pillars of marble: the beds were of gold and silver, upon a pavement of red, and blue, and white, and black, marble.", insight:"Gold and silver beds on a marble pavement; luxury is the scenery, not the point, of this chapter."},
{q:"What did the guests drink from at the feast?", options:["Vessels of gold, each one different from another","Silver cups, all alike","Wooden bowls","The king's own golden horn"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:7",verse:"And they gave them drink in vessels of gold, (the vessels being diverse one from another,) and royal wine in abundance, according to the state of the king.", insight:"No two vessels alike, and royal wine in abundance; extravagance measured everything except what mattered."},
{q:"What was the law concerning drinking at the feast?", options:["None did compel; every man drank according to his pleasure","Each guest must finish three cups","No wine after sunset","Only the nobles might drink"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:8",verse:"And the drinking was according to the law; none did compel: for so the king had appointed to all the officers of his house, that they should do according to every man’s pleasure.", insight:"Even a pagan king knew not to force the cup; compulsion spoils both wine and worship."},
{q:"While the king feasted, what did Queen Vashti do?", options:["Made a feast for the women in the royal house","Left the palace in secret","Sat silently beside the king","Refused to leave her chambers"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:9",verse:"Also Vashti the queen made a feast for the women in the royal house which belonged to king Ahasuerus.", insight:"Vashti kept her own feast for the women; her dignity stood apart from the king's display."},
{q:"On which day did the king send for Vashti?", options:["On the seventh day, when his heart was merry with wine","On the first day of the feast","On the Sabbath day","After the feast had ended"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:10",verse:"On the seventh day, when the heart of the king was merry with wine, he commanded Mehuman, Biztha, Harbona, Bigtha, and Abagtha, Zethar, and Carcas, the seven chamberlains that served in the presence of Ahasuerus the king,", insight:"The command came on the seventh day with a wine-merry heart; decisions made in drink rarely stand in daylight."},
{q:"Why did the king want Vashti brought before him?", options:["To show the people and the princes her beauty","To crown her again before them all","To ask her counsel about the law","To honor her father's house"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:11",verse:"To bring Vashti the queen before the king with the crown royal, to shew the people and the princes her beauty: for she was fair to look on.", insight:"She was to be shown like another treasure; beauty treated as property invites its own refusal."},
{q:"What did Queen Vashti do when summoned by the chamberlains?", options:["She refused to come at the king's commandment","She came but would not wear the crown","She delayed until the next day","She sent her sister in her place"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:12",verse:"But the queen Vashti refused to come at the king’s commandment by his chamberlains: therefore was the king very wroth, and his anger burned in him.", insight:"One refusal in a palace of yes-men; sometimes the bravest word is simply no."},
{q:"Whom did the king consult after Vashti's refusal?", options:["The wise men, which knew the times","His seven chamberlains","The captains of the army","The priests of Persia"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:13",verse:"Then the king said to the wise men, which knew the times, (for so was the king’s manner toward all that knew law and judgment:", insight:"He asked men who knew the times; knowing the times is useless if you do not know what is right."},
{q:"Who were the seven princes closest to the king?", options:["Those which saw the king's face and sat first in the kingdom","The governors of the provinces","The keepers of the treasury","The commanders of the guard"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:14",verse:"And the next unto him was Carshena, Shethar, Admatha, Tarshish, Meres, Marsena, and Memucan, the seven princes of Persia and Media, which saw the king’s face, and which sat the first in the kingdom;)", insight:"Seeing the king's face was the highest honor in Persia; nearness to power is not the same as wisdom."},
{q:"What question did the king put to his counselors?", options:["What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law?","Shall the feast continue another seven days?","Who shall be queen in Vashti's place?","How shall we punish the chamberlains?"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:15",verse:"What shall we do unto the queen Vashti according to law, because she hath not performed the commandment of the king Ahasuerus by the chamberlains?", insight:"He asked what the law required, not what was just; law without justice is only force in robes."},
{q:"Who answered the king before the princes?", options:["Memucan","Carshena","Shethar","Meres"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:16",verse:"And Memucan answered before the king and the princes, Vashti the queen hath not done wrong to the king only, but also to all the princes, and to all the people that are in all the provinces of the king Ahasuerus.", insight:"Memucan spoke for the frightened husbands of the empire; fear of losing face drove the whole decree."},
{q:"What did Memucan warn would happen if Vashti went unpunished?", options:["All women would despise their husbands in their eyes","The provinces would rebel","The army would desert","The priests would curse the king"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:17",verse:"For this deed of the queen shall come abroad unto all women, so that they shall despise their husbands in their eyes, when it shall be reported, The king Ahasuerus commanded Vashti the queen to be brought in before him, but she came not.", insight:"He feared every wife in the empire would follow her example; small acts of conscience terrify large systems of control."},
{q:"What did the royal decree command concerning Vashti?", options:["That she come no more before the king, and her royal estate be given to another","That she be imprisoned for a year","That she be sent back to her father's house","That she be fined ten talents of silver"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:19",verse:"If it please the king, let there go a royal commandment from him, and let it be written among the laws of the Persians and the Medes, that it be not altered, That Vashti come no more before king Ahasuerus; and let the king give her royal estate unto another that is better than she.", insight:"A law of the Medes and Persians could not be altered; God would use even unchangeable law to open a door for Esther."},
{q:"When the decree was published, what would all the wives do?", options:["Give to their husbands honour, both to great and small","Leave their homes in protest","Send gifts to the queen","Assemble yearly at Shushan"], a:0, ref:"Esther 1:20",verse:"And when the king’s decree which he shall make shall be published throughout all his empire, (for it is great,) all the wives shall give to their husbands honour, both to great and small.", insight:"An empire commanded what only love can give; honour forced by decree is not honour at all."}
 ]},
{n:2, name:"Esther Crowned",
 seal:{ref:"Esther 2:17",verse:"And the king loved Esther above all the women, and she obtained grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown upon her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti."},
 facts:["Did you know Hadassah, Esther's Hebrew name, means 'myrtle,' a tree whose leaves stay green and fragrant even when crushed (Esther 2:7)?","Did you know each maiden spent twelve full months in purification, six months with oil of myrrh and six months with sweet odours, before ever seeing the king (Esther 2:12)?","Did you know Mordecai's report of the plot against the king was written in the book of the chronicles, a record that would matter greatly later in the story (Esther 2:23)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"After his anger cooled, what did Ahasuerus do?", options:["He remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed","He sent for Vashti at once","He forgot the whole matter","He punished Memucan"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:1",verse:"After these things, when the wrath of king Ahasuerus was appeased, he remembered Vashti, and what she had done, and what was decreed against her.", insight:"He remembered her when the wine wore off; regret that comes too late still shapes what comes next."},
{q:"What did the king's servants propose?", options:["Let fair young virgins be sought for the king","Let the king remarry Vashti","Let a bride be chosen from Media","Let the king wait a year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:2",verse:"Then said the king’s servants that ministered unto him, Let there be fair young virgins sought for the king:", insight:"Servants flattered a king's appetite to keep his favor; counsel that feeds desire is not counsel."},
{q:"Who was given custody of the gathered maidens?", options:["Hege the king's chamberlain, keeper of the women","Shaashgaz, keeper of the concubines","Memucan the prince","Hatach the attendant"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:3",verse:"And let the king appoint officers in all the provinces of his kingdom, that they may gather together all the fair young virgins unto Shushan the palace, to the house of the women unto the custody of Hege the king’s chamberlain, keeper of the women; and let their things for purification be given them:", insight:"The search was organized by officers across every province; God let Esther be gathered by the very system that would serve Him."},
{q:"Who was Mordecai?", options:["A Jew of the tribe of Benjamin, the son of Jair","A prince of Media","A Persian governor","A Babylonian scribe"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:5",verse:"Now in Shushan the palace there was a certain Jew, whose name was Mordecai, the son of Jair, the son of Shimei, the son of Kish, a Benjamite;", insight:"Scripture traces his line back to Kish, Saul's father; the Benjamite seed was planted for this hour."},
{q:"How had Mordecai's family come to Persia?", options:["They were carried away from Jerusalem in the captivity under Nebuchadnezzar","They fled Egypt with Moses","They migrated for trade","They came as ambassadors"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:6",verse:"Who had been carried away from Jerusalem with the captivity which had been carried away with Jeconiah king of Judah, whom Nebuchadnezzar the king of Babylon had carried away.", insight:"Exile put Mordecai's family in Shushan; God had been positioning His pieces for generations."},
{q:"Who was Hadassah?", options:["Mordecai's uncle's daughter, whom he raised as his own daughter","A Persian princess","The king's niece","A servant in the women's house"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:7",verse:"And he brought up Hadassah, that is, Esther, his uncle’s daughter: for she had neither father nor mother, and the maid was fair and beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her father and mother were dead, took for his own daughter.", insight:"Hadassah, that is Esther; an orphan girl raised by her cousin would carry a nation's fate."},
{q:"Why did Mordecai take Esther for his own daughter?", options:["She had neither father nor mother","She was his only heir","The king commanded it","She was betrothed to his son"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:7",verse:"And he brought up Hadassah, that is, Esther, his uncle’s daughter: for she had neither father nor mother, and the maid was fair and beautiful; whom Mordecai, when her father and mother were dead, took for his own daughter.", insight:"Orphaned and adopted; God often raises His deliverers in quiet, borrowed homes."},
{q:"Where was Esther placed when she was taken to the palace?", options:["In the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women","In the house of the concubines","In Vashti's old chambers","In the king's own house at once"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:8",verse:"So it came to pass, when the king’s commandment and his decree was heard, and when many maidens were gathered together unto Shushan the palace, to the custody of Hegai, that Esther was brought also unto the king’s house, to the custody of Hegai, keeper of the women.", insight:"She entered the system that consumed women; favour, not force, would set her apart."},
{q:"How did Hegai treat Esther?", options:["He speedily gave her purification things, seven maidens, and the best place","He ignored her among the others","He made her serve the other maidens","He sent her back home"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:9",verse:"And the maiden pleased him, and she obtained kindness of him; and he speedily gave her her things for purification, with such things as belonged to her, and seven maidens, which were meet to be given her, out of the king’s house: and he preferred her and her maids unto the best place of the house of the women.", insight:"She obtained kindness before she obtained the crown; favour opens doors that striving cannot."},
{q:"What had Mordecai charged Esther not to reveal?", options:["Her people and her kindred","Her name Hadassah","Her age","Where she was born"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:10",verse:"Esther had not shewed her people nor her kindred: for Mordecai had charged her that she should not shew it.", insight:"Silence was her shield; God sometimes hides His people until the revealing hour."},
{q:"What did Mordecai do every day?", options:["Walked before the court of the women's house to know how Esther did","Sat in the king's gate","Prayed in the synagogue","Worked in the palace kitchens"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:11",verse:"And Mordecai walked every day before the court of the women’s house, to know how Esther did, and what should become of her.", insight:"A father's daily walk past the gate; watchful love is a quiet form of courage."},
{q:"How long did each maiden's purification last?", options:["Twelve months, six with oil of myrrh and six with sweet odours","Thirty days","Forty days","One full year of fasting"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:12",verse:"Now when every maid’s turn was come to go in to king Ahasuerus, after that she had been twelve months, according to the manner of the women, (for so were the days of their purifications accomplished, to wit, six months with oil of myrrh, and six months with sweet odours, and with other things for the purifying of the women;)", insight:"Twelve months of preparation for one night with the king; the world prepared her body while God prepared her purpose."},
{q:"After going in to the king, where did a maiden return?", options:["To the second house of the women, under Shaashgaz, keeper of the concubines","To her own province","To the first house again","To the king's gate"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:14",verse:"In the evening she went, and on the morrow she returned into the second house of the women, to the custody of Shaashgaz, the king’s chamberlain, which kept the concubines: she came in unto the king no more, except the king delighted in her, and that she were called by name.", insight:"She came in no more unless called by name; being summoned by the king was rare, and Esther would need that summons."},
{q:"What did Esther request when her turn came to go in?", options:["Nothing but what Hegai appointed","The finest robes in the house","Jewels above all the others","A feast for the king"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:15",verse:"Now when the turn of Esther, the daughter of Abihail the uncle of Mordecai, who had taken her for his daughter, was come to go in unto the king, she required nothing but what Hegai the king’s chamberlain, the keeper of the women, appointed. And Esther obtained favour in the sight of all them that looked upon her.", insight:"She required nothing of her own; restraint stood out in a house built on self-display."},
{q:"In which month and year was Esther taken to the king?", options:["The tenth month, Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign","The first month, Nisan, in the third year","The twelfth month, Adar, in the twelfth year","The sixth month, in the fifth year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:16",verse:"So Esther was taken unto king Ahasuerus into his house royal in the tenth month, which is the month Tebeth, in the seventh year of his reign.", insight:"Four years after Vashti's fall, God's timing placed Esther on the throne before Haman's plot existed."},
{q:"How did the king receive Esther?", options:["He loved her above all the women and set the royal crown on her head","He chose her as one concubine among many","He sent her back to the women's house","He made her serve Vashti's memory"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:17",verse:"And the king loved Esther above all the women, and she obtained grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; so that he set the royal crown upon her head, and made her queen instead of Vashti.", insight:"Grace and favour in his sight more than all the virgins; favour is God's signature on the unlikely."},
{q:"What did the king do to celebrate Esther?", options:["Made a great feast, a release to the provinces, and gave gifts","Built her a new palace","Declared a month of rest","Doubled the taxes"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:18",verse:"Then the king made a great feast unto all his princes and his servants, even Esther’s feast; and he made a release to the provinces, and gave gifts, according to the state of the king.", insight:"Esther's feast brought release and gifts to the provinces; a queen's joy overflowed to the whole empire."},
{q:"Where was Mordecai when the virgins were gathered the second time?", options:["Sitting in the king's gate","Walking before the women's house","In the palace prison","At the city market"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:19",verse:"And when the virgins were gathered together the second time, then Mordecai sat in the king’s gate.", insight:"From the gate he watched over Esther; lowly posts become listening posts in God's hands."},
{q:"What did Bigthan and Teresh plan?", options:["To lay hand on King Ahasuerus","To poison the queen","To free Vashti","To burn the palace"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:21",verse:"In those days, while Mordecai sat in the king’s gate, two of the king’s chamberlains, Bigthan and Teresh, of those which kept the door, were wroth, and sought to lay hand on the king Ahasuerus.", insight:"Two doorkeepers plotted murder at the gate where Mordecai sat; God places His witnesses where treason whispers."},
{q:"What happened to the two plotters?", options:["They were hanged on a tree, and it was written in the chronicles","They were pardoned","They fled to Egypt","They were made eunuchs"], a:0, ref:"Esther 2:23",verse:"And when inquisition was made of the matter, it was found out; therefore they were both hanged on a tree: and it was written in the book of the chronicles before the king.", insight:"Justice was done and recorded; a forgotten entry in the chronicles would one day save a nation."}
 ]},
{n:3, name:"Haman's Plot",
 seal:{ref:"Esther 3:6",verse:"And he thought scorn to lay hands on Mordecai alone; for they had shewed him the people of Mordecai: wherefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews that were throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even the people of Mordecai."},
 facts:["Did you know 'Pur' means 'the lot,' and the feast of Purim later took its name from the lots Haman cast to choose the day of slaughter (Esther 3:7)?","Did you know Haman is called 'the Jews' enemy,' one of the starkest titles given to any man in Scripture (Esther 3:10)?","Did you know ten thousand talents of silver was an enormous fortune, yet Haman offered it freely to fund the destruction of the Jews (Esther 3:9)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"Whom did Ahasuerus promote above all the princes?", options:["Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite","Memucan the counselor","Mordecai the Jew","Hege the chamberlain"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:1",verse:"After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that were with him.", insight:"The enemy rose to the highest seat; God lets the proud climb so the fall is seen by all."},
{q:"What title follows Haman's name in Scripture?", options:["The Agagite","The Persian","The Mede","The Babylonian"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:1",verse:"After these things did king Ahasuerus promote Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, and advanced him, and set his seat above all the princes that were with him.", insight:"Agag was king of Amalek, Israel's ancient foe; old hatreds wear new robes in every generation."},
{q:"What did the king's servants at the gate do to Haman?", options:["Bowed and reverenced him","Refused to serve him","Laughed at him","Reported him to the king"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:2",verse:"And all the king’s servants, that were in the king’s gate, bowed, and reverenced Haman: for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence.", insight:"All bowed because the king commanded it; commanded reverence is flattery, not honour."},
{q:"What did Mordecai refuse to do?", options:["Bow to Haman or do him reverence","Serve at the king's gate","Pay the king's tax","Speak to the servants"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:2",verse:"And all the king’s servants, that were in the king’s gate, bowed, and reverenced Haman: for the king had so commanded concerning him. But Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence.", insight:"One unbending knee in a courtyard of bowed heads; conscience does not kneel to pride."},
{q:"What did the servants ask Mordecai?", options:["Why transgressest thou the king's commandment?","Why sittest thou in the gate?","Why hidest thou thy people?","Why mournest thou in sackcloth?"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:3",verse:"Then the king’s servants, which were in the king’s gate, said unto Mordecai, Why transgressest thou the king’s commandment?", insight:"They measured him by the king's commandment; Mordecai measured himself by a higher law."},
{q:"Why did the servants tell Haman about Mordecai?", options:["To see whether Mordecai's matters would stand, for he had told them he was a Jew","To win Haman's favor","To have Mordecai arrested","To test the king's decree"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:4",verse:"Now it came to pass, when they spake daily unto him, and he hearkened not unto them, that they told Haman, to see whether Mordecai’s matters would stand: for he had told them that he was a Jew.", insight:"They spake daily unto him and he hearkened not; persistent pressure still meets a settled conscience."},
{q:"How did Haman react when he saw Mordecai would not bow?", options:["He was full of wrath","He laughed it off","He reported it calmly to the king","He pitied him"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:5",verse:"And when Haman saw that Mordecai bowed not, nor did him reverence, then was Haman full of wrath.", insight:"Full of wrath at one man's stillness; pride cannot bear a single exception."},
{q:"Why did Haman scorn to attack Mordecai alone?", options:["Because they had shown him Mordecai's people, so he sought to destroy all the Jews","Because Mordecai was protected by the king","Because he feared the gate servants","Because the law forbade it"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:6",verse:"And he thought scorn to lay hands on Mordecai alone; for they had shewed him the people of Mordecai: wherefore Haman sought to destroy all the Jews that were throughout the whole kingdom of Ahasuerus, even the people of Mordecai.", insight:"One man's dignity condemned a whole people in Haman's eyes; hatred never stops at one."},
{q:"What was cast before Haman?", options:["Pur, that is, the lot","Dice of gold","The king's ring","Stones of judgment"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:7",verse:"In the first month, that is, the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that is, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, to the twelfth month, that is, the month Adar.", insight:"They cast the lot to choose the day of murder; men cast lots, but the disposing belongs to the Lord."},
{q:"In which year of Ahasuerus was the lot cast?", options:["The twelfth year","The third year","The seventh year","The first year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:7",verse:"In the first month, that is, the month Nisan, in the twelfth year of king Ahasuerus, they cast Pur, that is, the lot, before Haman from day to day, and from month to month, to the twelfth month, that is, the month Adar.", insight:"Twelve years into the reign the plot ripened; evil takes time to arrange what God overturns in a night."},
{q:"How did Haman describe the Jews to the king?", options:["Scattered abroad and dispersed, with laws diverse from all people","Rebels plotting war","Thieves robbing the treasury","Spies for a foreign king"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:8",verse:"And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus, There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the people in all the provinces of thy kingdom; and their laws are diverse from all people; neither keep they the king’s laws: therefore it is not for the king’s profit to suffer them.", insight:"Scattered, diverse, not keeping the king's laws; every persecution begins with a description that makes a people sound dangerous."},
{q:"What did Haman claim about the Jews' laws?", options:["They were diverse from all people, and they kept not the king's laws","They were stolen from Babylon","They commanded rebellion","They forbade paying taxes"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:8",verse:"And Haman said unto king Ahasuerus, There is a certain people scattered abroad and dispersed among the people in all the provinces of thy kingdom; and their laws are diverse from all people; neither keep they the king’s laws: therefore it is not for the king’s profit to suffer them.", insight:"Their laws are diverse from all people; difference is not disloyalty, though tyrants call it so."},
{q:"How much silver did Haman offer to pay into the king's treasuries?", options:["Ten thousand talents","One thousand talents","A hundred talents","Ten talents"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:9",verse:"If it please the king, let it be written that they may be destroyed: and I will pay ten thousand talents of silver to the hands of those that have the charge of the business, to bring it into the king’s treasuries.", insight:"Ten thousand talents to fund a genocide; evil will bankrupt itself to buy what God will not sell."},
{q:"What did the king give to Haman?", options:["His ring from his hand","His golden sceptre","His royal crown","His signet chain"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:10",verse:"And the king took his ring from his hand, and gave it unto Haman the son of Hammedatha the Agagite, the Jews’ enemy.", insight:"The ring was the king's own authority; careless power signs what it has not read."},
{q:"What did the king say when he gave Haman the ring?", options:["The silver is given to thee, the people also, to do with them as it seemeth good to thee","Guard the Jews with thy life","Bring the silver to my treasury","Ask my counsel first"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:11",verse:"And the king said unto Haman, The silver is given to thee, the people also, to do with them as it seemeth good to thee.", insight:"Do as it seemeth good to thee; a king who will not govern hands his people to whoever will."},
{q:"On which day were the king's scribes called to write the decree?", options:["The thirteenth day of the first month","The first day of Nisan","The thirteenth day of Adar","The last day of the year"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:12",verse:"Then were the king’s scribes called on the thirteenth day of the first month, and there was written according to all that Haman had commanded unto the king’s lieutenants, and to the governors that were over every province, and to the rulers of every people of every province according to the writing thereof, and to every people after their language; in the name of king Ahasuerus was it written, and sealed with the king’s ring.", insight:"Written in the king's name and sealed with his ring; an irreversible law was being aimed at God's people."},
{q:"What did the letters command against the Jews?", options:["To destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, young and old","To drive them from the provinces","To tax them double","To imprison their leaders"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:13",verse:"And the letters were sent by posts into all the king’s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, even upon the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and to take the spoil of them for a prey.", insight:"Destroy, kill, perish, all, young and old, little children and women; hatred drafts its orders without mercy."},
{q:"On what day was the slaughter appointed?", options:["The thirteenth day of the twelfth month, Adar","The thirteenth day of the first month","The last day of the year","The feast of Purim"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:13",verse:"And the letters were sent by posts into all the king’s provinces, to destroy, to kill, and to cause to perish, all Jews, both young and old, little children and women, in one day, even upon the thirteenth day of the twelfth month, which is the month Adar, and to take the spoil of them for a prey.", insight:"Nearly a year of waiting was built into the decree; God uses the delay to prepare the rescue."},
{q:"What was published with the copy of the decree?", options:["That all people should be ready against that day","That the Jews should flee","That Haman was promoted","That the king repented"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:14",verse:"The copy of the writing for a commandment to be given in every province was published unto all people, that they should be ready against that day.", insight:"Every province was told to be ready; evil organizes openly when no one stands against it."},
{q:"What contrast ends the chapter?", options:["The king and Haman sat down to drink, but the city Shushan was perplexed","The Jews fled the city in terror","Mordecai confronted Haman","Esther wept in the palace"], a:0, ref:"Esther 3:15",verse:"The posts went out, being hastened by the king’s commandment, and the decree was given in Shushan the palace. And the king and Haman sat down to drink; but the city Shushan was perplexed.", insight:"Two men drank while a city trembled; indifference at the top is felt as terror below."}
 ]},
{n:4, name:"For Such a Time as This",
 seal:{ref:"Esther 4:14",verse:"For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, then shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father’s house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?"},
 facts:["Did you know Esther's words 'if I perish, I perish' are among the most quoted lines in the book, spoken as she chose to risk her life for her people (Esther 4:16)?","Did you know Mordecai's challenge, 'who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this,' has become a classic call to courage in God's providence (Esther 4:14)?","Did you know that in every province the Jews answered the decree with fasting, weeping, and wailing, and many lay in sackcloth and ashes, turning to God before any rescue came (Esther 4:3)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"What did Mordecai do when he perceived all that was done?", options:["Rent his clothes, put on sackcloth with ashes, and cried with a loud and bitter cry","Fled the city","Confronted Haman","Wrote to Esther at once"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:1",verse:"When Mordecai perceived all that was done, Mordecai rent his clothes, and put on sackcloth with ashes, and went out into the midst of the city, and cried with a loud and a bitter cry;", insight:"His cry went out into the midst of the city; grief that will not hide is the beginning of intercession."},
{q:"Why did Mordecai stop before the king's gate?", options:["None might enter the king's gate clothed with sackcloth","The guards turned him away","He feared Haman","The gate was closed"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:2",verse:"And came even before the king’s gate: for none might enter into the king’s gate clothed with sackcloth.", insight:"Sorrow could come no nearer to power; the gate that shut out sackcloth would soon admit Esther."},
{q:"What spread among the Jews in every province?", options:["Great mourning, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing","Joy and feasting","Silence and hiding","Anger and rioting"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:3",verse:"And in every province, whithersoever the king’s commandment and his decree came, there was great mourning among the Jews, and fasting, and weeping, and wailing; and many lay in sackcloth and ashes.", insight:"Fasting, weeping, and many lay in sackcloth and ashes; a whole people turned to God before they turned to the queen."},
{q:"What did Esther do when she heard of Mordecai?", options:["She was exceedingly grieved and sent raiment to clothe him","She summoned him to the palace","She ignored the report","She sent for Haman"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:4",verse:"So Esther’s maids and her chamberlains came and told it her. Then was the queen exceedingly grieved; and she sent raiment to clothe Mordecai, and to take away his sackcloth from him: but he received it not.", insight:"She sent clothes to take away his sackcloth; comfort that removes the sign of grief does not remove the cause."},
{q:"Did Mordecai accept the clothes Esther sent?", options:["No, he received them not","Yes, and put them on at once","Yes, but he stayed outside","He sent them back with thanks"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:4",verse:"So Esther’s maids and her chamberlains came and told it her. Then was the queen exceedingly grieved; and she sent raiment to clothe Mordecai, and to take away his sackcloth from him: but he received it not.", insight:"He received it not; some griefs refuse covering until the danger passes."},
{q:"Whom did Esther send to learn what troubled Mordecai?", options:["Hatach, one of the king's chamberlains appointed to attend her","Hegai the keeper of the women","Bigthan the doorkeeper","A maiden from her household"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:5",verse:"Then called Esther for Hatach, one of the king’s chamberlains, whom he had appointed to attend upon her, and gave him a commandment to Mordecai, to know what it was, and why it was.", insight:"She sent her own attendant to the gate; the queen's first step was to listen."},
{q:"Where did Hatach meet Mordecai?", options:["In the street of the city, before the king's gate","In the palace court","At Mordecai's house","In the women's house"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:6",verse:"So Hatach went forth to Mordecai unto the street of the city, which was before the king’s gate.", insight:"The street before the gate became a council chamber; God's plans are laid in humble places."},
{q:"What did Mordecai tell Hatach about Haman's bargain?", options:["The sum of the money Haman had promised to pay for the Jews' destruction","The day the lots were cast","The names of Haman's sons","The route of the posts"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:7",verse:"And Mordecai told him of all that had happened unto him, and of the sum of the money that Haman had promised to pay to the king’s treasuries for the Jews, to destroy them.", insight:"He named the price on his people's heads; facing the facts plainly is the first act of faith."},
{q:"What did Mordecai send to Esther with Hatach?", options:["A copy of the decree, with a charge to go to the king and plead for her people","A letter of farewell","The king's ring","A plan of escape"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:8",verse:"Also he gave him the copy of the writing of the decree that was given at Shushan to destroy them, to shew it unto Esther, and to declare it unto her, and to charge her that she should go in unto the king, to make supplication unto him, and to make request before him for her people.", insight:"The copy of the decree in her hands made it real; faith acts on evidence, not on feeling."},
{q:"What did Hatach do when he returned to Esther?", options:["He told Esther the words of Mordecai","He hid the decree","He warned Haman","He stayed silent"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:9",verse:"And Hatach came and told Esther the words of Mordecai.", insight:"He told Esther the words of Mordecai; faithful messengers carry hard words straight."},
{q:"What did Esther send back to Mordecai first?", options:["She spake unto Hatach and gave him commandment unto Mordecai","A gift of silver","A new plan","Her crown"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:10",verse:"Again Esther spake unto Hatach, and gave him commandment unto Mordecai;", insight:"She answered through her messenger; even queens must speak through the narrow gates God opens."},
{q:"What law did Esther remind Mordecai of?", options:["Whoever comes to the king unsummoned is put to death, unless he holds out the golden sceptre","No queen may leave the palace","No Jew may enter the inner court","The king may not be approached at night"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:11",verse:"All the king’s servants, and the people of the king’s provinces, do know, that whosoever, whether man or woman, shall come unto the king into the inner court, who is not called, there is one law of his to put him to death, except such to whom the king shall hold out the golden sceptre, that he may live: but I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.", insight:"One law for man or woman: death, unless the sceptre lifts; Esther counted the cost before she chose."},
{q:"How long had it been since Esther was called to the king?", options:["Thirty days","Seven days","A full year","Three days"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:11",verse:"All the king’s servants, and the people of the king’s provinces, do know, that whosoever, whether man or woman, shall come unto the king into the inner court, who is not called, there is one law of his to put him to death, except such to whom the king shall hold out the golden sceptre, that he may live: but I have not been called to come in unto the king these thirty days.", insight:"Thirty days uncalled; favour can cool, and she knew the risk was real."},
{q:"What warning did Mordecai send back to Esther?", options:["Think not that thou shalt escape in the king's house more than all the Jews","Flee to Jerusalem","Hide thy kindred still","Wait for a better time"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:13",verse:"Then Mordecai commanded to answer Esther, Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king’s house, more than all the Jews.", insight:"The palace was no shelter; safety that abandons duty is no safety at all."},
{q:"What did Mordecai say would happen to Esther if she did nothing?", options:["She and her father's house would be destroyed","She would be divorced like Vashti","She would be exiled to Jerusalem","She would lose her maids"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:13",verse:"Then Mordecai commanded to answer Esther, Think not with thyself that thou shalt escape in the king’s house, more than all the Jews.", insight:"Thou and thy father's house shall be destroyed; silence in the face of evil is never neutral."},
{q:"What did Mordecai say would happen if Esther stayed silent?", options:["Enlargement and deliverance would arise to the Jews from another place","The decree would be forgotten","Haman would show mercy","The king would remember Vashti"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:14",verse:"For if thou altogether holdest thy peace at this time, then shall there enlargement and deliverance arise to the Jews from another place; but thou and thy father’s house shall be destroyed: and who knoweth whether thou art come to the kingdom for such a time as this?", insight:"God's deliverance does not depend on us, but our part in it does; He will save His people, with or without us."},
{q:"What did Esther do when she heard Mordecai's warning?", options:["She bade them return Mordecai this answer","She wept and did nothing","She sent for the king","She fled the palace"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:15",verse:"Then Esther bade them return Mordecai this answer,", insight:"She answered, not with argument but with resolve; conviction moves quickly once it is settled."},
{q:"What was Esther's first instruction to Mordecai?", options:["Go, gather all the Jews in Shushan and fast for me three days","Go to the king at once","Write to Haman","Pray alone tonight"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:16",verse:"Go, gather together all the Jews that are present in Shushan, and fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day: I also and my maidens will fast likewise; and so will I go in unto the king, which is not according to the law: and if I perish, I perish.", insight:"Gather, fast, three days, night and day; before she faced the king she gathered the prayers of her people."},
{q:"What did Esther resolve to do?", options:["Go in unto the king, though not according to the law; and if I perish, I perish","Wait until she was called","Send a letter by Hatach","Appeal to the princes"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:16",verse:"Go, gather together all the Jews that are present in Shushan, and fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink three days, night or day: I also and my maidens will fast likewise; and so will I go in unto the king, which is not according to the law: and if I perish, I perish.", insight:"If I perish, I perish; courage is not the absence of fear but obedience in spite of it."},
{q:"What did Mordecai do then?", options:["He went his way and did according to all that Esther had commanded him","He argued with her","He went to Haman","He left Shushan"], a:0, ref:"Esther 4:17",verse:"So Mordecai went his way, and did according to all that Esther had commanded him.", insight:"He did all that she commanded him; the older counselor obeyed the younger queen, and God honored them both."}
 ]},
{n:5, name:"The First Banquet",
 seal:{ref:"Esther 5:13",verse:"Yet all this availeth me nothing, so long as I see Mordecai the Jew sitting at the king’s gate."},
 facts:["Did you know the gallows Haman built stood fifty cubits high, about seventy-five feet, a towering monument to his hatred (Esther 5:14)?","Did you know Esther invited Haman to not one but two banquets, waiting until the second to reveal her petition (Esther 5:4, 8)?","Did you know 'to the half of the kingdom' was a royal formula of extravagant generosity, offered to Esther twice in this chapter (Esther 5:3, 6)?"],
 questions:[
{q:"On which day did Esther act?", options:["On the third day","On the seventh day","After forty days","The next morning"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:1",verse:"Now it came to pass on the third day, that Esther put on her royal apparel, and stood in the inner court of the king’s house, over against the king’s house: and the king sat upon his royal throne in the royal house, over against the gate of the house.", insight:"The third day, after three days of fasting; prayer first, then the palace."},
{q:"How did Esther appear before the king?", options:["In her royal apparel, standing in the inner court","In sackcloth, weeping","In a servant's dress","Veiled and silent"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:1",verse:"Now it came to pass on the third day, that Esther put on her royal apparel, and stood in the inner court of the king’s house, over against the king’s house: and the king sat upon his royal throne in the royal house, over against the gate of the house.", insight:"Royal apparel, not sackcloth; she came as a queen, trusting God with the outcome."},
{q:"What did the king hold out to Esther?", options:["The golden sceptre that was in his hand","His hand","His ring","A cup of wine"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:2",verse:"And it was so, when the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, that she obtained favour in his sight: and the king held out to Esther the golden sceptre that was in his hand. So Esther drew near, and touched the top of the sceptre.", insight:"The golden sceptre lifted; one gesture turned a death sentence into favour."},
{q:"What did Esther do when the sceptre was held out?", options:["She drew near and touched the top of the sceptre","She bowed to the ground","She wept aloud","She turned to leave"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:2",verse:"And it was so, when the king saw Esther the queen standing in the court, that she obtained favour in his sight: and the king held out to Esther the golden sceptre that was in his hand. So Esther drew near, and touched the top of the sceptre.", insight:"She touched the top of the sceptre; small acts of faith receive great mercies."},
{q:"What did the king ask Esther?", options:["What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is thy request?","Why hast thou come uncalled?","Who sent thee hither?","What troubles thee, my queen?"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:3",verse:"Then said the king unto her, What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is thy request? it shall be even given thee to the half of the kingdom.", insight:"What wilt thou; the most powerful man in the empire opened his hand to her."},
{q:"How far did the king's offer go?", options:["Even to the half of the kingdom","To a hundred talents","To any province she chose","To Haman's estate"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:3",verse:"Then said the king unto her, What wilt thou, queen Esther? and what is thy request? it shall be even given thee to the half of the kingdom.", insight:"To the half of the kingdom; extravagant offers test whether we want things or God's will."},
{q:"Whom did Esther invite to her banquet?", options:["The king and Haman","The seven princes","Mordecai and Hatach","The queen's maidens"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:4",verse:"And Esther answered, If it seem good unto the king, let the king and Haman come this day unto the banquet that I have prepared for him.", insight:"The king and Haman, this day; she set the table before she sprang the truth."},
{q:"For which day did Esther invite the king and Haman?", options:["This day","The next Sabbath","The feast of Purim","A month later"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:4",verse:"And Esther answered, If it seem good unto the king, let the king and Haman come this day unto the banquet that I have prepared for him.", insight:"This day; when God gives the moment, Esther did not delay."},
{q:"What did the king say when he heard Esther's invitation?", options:["Cause Haman to make haste, that he may do as Esther hath said","Prepare a greater feast","Summon the princes also","Ask her request now"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:5",verse:"Then the king said, Cause Haman to make haste, that he may do as Esther hath said. So the king and Haman came to the banquet that Esther had prepared.", insight:"Cause Haman to make haste; the enemy hurried to the very banquet that would undo him."},
{q:"What did the king ask at the banquet of wine?", options:["What is thy petition? and it shall be granted thee","Why is Haman here?","What troubles the city?","Shall I make thy request law?"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:6",verse:"And the king said unto Esther at the banquet of wine, What is thy petition? and it shall be granted thee: and what is thy request? even to the half of the kingdom it shall be performed.", insight:"At the banquet of wine he asked again; Esther held her petition for the fuller moment."},
{q:"How did Esther begin her answer?", options:["My petition and my request is","O king, hear me","I am a Jew","Haman is wicked"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:7",verse:"Then answered Esther, and said, My petition and my request is;", insight:"My petition and my request is; she named what she wanted before she named whom she feared."},
{q:"What did Esther ask the king to do?", options:["Come again tomorrow to another banquet she would prepare","Decide her petition at once","Banish Haman tonight","Call Mordecai"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:8",verse:"If I have found favour in the sight of the king, and if it please the king to grant my petition, and to perform my request, let the king and Haman come to the banquet that I shall prepare for them, and I will do to morrow as the king hath said.", insight:"One more banquet tomorrow; patience in God's plan is not delay but design."},
{q:"How did Haman leave the banquet?", options:["Joyful and with a glad heart","Fearful and trembling","Angry at the king","Suspicious of Esther"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:9",verse:"Then went Haman forth that day joyful and with a glad heart: but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king’s gate, that he stood not up, nor moved for him, he was full of indignation against Mordecai.", insight:"Joyful and glad of heart; pride feasts the night before it falls."},
{q:"What turned Haman's joy to indignation?", options:["Seeing Mordecai in the king's gate, who stood not up nor moved for him","A rebuke from the king","Bad news from home","Esther's cold farewell"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:9",verse:"Then went Haman forth that day joyful and with a glad heart: but when Haman saw Mordecai in the king’s gate, that he stood not up, nor moved for him, he was full of indignation against Mordecai.", insight:"Mordecai stood not up, nor moved for him; one unmoved man unraveled all his joy."},
{q:"What did Haman do when he came home?", options:["Refrained himself, and called his friends and Zeresh his wife","Wept before them","Sent for Mordecai","Drank until midnight"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:10",verse:"Nevertheless Haman refrained himself: and when he came home, he sent and called for his friends, and Zeresh his wife.", insight:"He refrained himself, then boasted at home; restrained anger curdles into plotted revenge."},
{q:"Of what did Haman boast to his friends?", options:["The glory of his riches and the multitude of his children","His wisdom above the princes","His armies","His new palace"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:11",verse:"And Haman told them of the glory of his riches, and the multitude of his children, and all the things wherein the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.", insight:"Riches and many children, counted aloud; boasting inventories what God can scatter."},
{q:"How had the king advanced Haman, by his own telling?", options:["Above the princes and servants of the king","Above the queen herself","To ruler of Shushan","To keeper of the treasury"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:11",verse:"And Haman told them of the glory of his riches, and the multitude of his children, and all the things wherein the king had promoted him, and how he had advanced him above the princes and servants of the king.", insight:"Advanced above all the princes; the higher pride climbs, the harder the reckoning."},
{q:"Who else did Esther invite to her banquet, according to Haman?", options:["No man but himself with the king","All the princes","Mordecai the Jew","The seven chamberlains"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:12",verse:"Haman said moreover, Yea, Esther the queen did let no man come in with the king unto the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and to morrow am I invited unto her also with the king.", insight:"No man but myself; being the only guest fed the very pride that would hang him."},
{q:"What honor did Haman expect the next day?", options:["To be invited again with the king to Esther's banquet","To be crowned prince","To receive the king's ring","To sit on the throne"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:12",verse:"Haman said moreover, Yea, Esther the queen did let no man come in with the king unto the banquet that she had prepared but myself; and to morrow am I invited unto her also with the king.", insight:"Tomorrow with the king; he counted honors that were already turning to gallows."},
{q:"What did Zeresh and his friends advise?", options:["Make a gallows fifty cubits high and ask the king to hang Mordecai on it","Poison Mordecai's food","Have Mordecai arrested","Bribe the gatekeepers"], a:0, ref:"Esther 5:14",verse:"Then said Zeresh his wife and all his friends unto him, Let a gallows be made of fifty cubits high, and to morrow speak thou unto the king that Mordecai may be hanged thereon: then go thou in merrily with the king unto the banquet. And the thing pleased Haman; and he caused the gallows to be made.", insight:"Fifty cubits high, built that night; the gallows rose before the reason for it fell."}
 ]}
]);
